        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Atmel/ AVR/ATtiny-centric boards: ... an ATtiny-driven fan controller"}
      ],
      "impact": "If U2 is populated, the PB3/PB4 signals are swapped relative to the ATtiny13 part, so the pot/ADC/control/PWM paths are misassigned. If both U1 and U2 are populated, their PB3/PB4 pins are cross-coupled and may drive each other.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a pinout mismatch: the ATtiny13 footprint U2 is wired with the ATtiny45 PB3/PB4 pin assignment, so U2 would have PB3 and PB4 swapped if populated."
}

